#
# Placeholder kernel configuration for Fairphone 5 (QCM6490)
#
# This config must be generated from a real kernel build:
#
#   1. Start from qcom_defconfig:
#      make ARCH=arm64 qcom_defconfig
#
#   2. Use menuconfig to enable Mobile NixOS requirements:
#      bin/menuconfig fairphone-fp5
#
#   3. Normalize the config:
#      bin/kernel-normalize-config fairphone-fp5
#
# Key options that must be enabled for the FP5:
#   - CONFIG_ARCH_QCOM=y
#   - CONFIG_DRM_MSM=y (or m)
#   - CONFIG_QCOM_* (various Qualcomm subsystem drivers)
#   - CONFIG_USB_DWC3=y/m (USB controller)
#   - CONFIG_PHY_QCOM_QMP=y/m
#   - CONFIG_TYPEC=y/m (USB-C)
#   - CONFIG_I2C_QCOM_GENI=y/m
#   - CONFIG_SPI_QCOM_GENI=y/m
#   - CONFIG_SERIAL_MSM=y (serial console)
#   - CONFIG_SERIAL_MSM_CONSOLE=y
#   - CONFIG_PINCTRL_QCM6490=y
#   - CONFIG_QCOM_PDC=y
#   - CONFIG_UFS_QCOM=y/m (storage)
#
# See postmarketOS linux-fairphone-fp5 APKBUILD for additional reference.
#
